Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Activation Transaction P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] bd7bb454-28c2-4625-bba8-7cf564986bf7
@ [canonical_uuid] 28da111f-c6b2-4df7-b708-a2d47f8e0bbb

& [Decision]
  + implement pure SWA-06B2A transaction admission before any physical source reacquisition registry persistence or current-SOP activation

& [Why]
  + SWA-06B1 closes cryptographic review correspondence but deliberately leaves six physical obligations open
  + a fully bound transaction makes the eventual writer small auditable stale-state-sensitive and recovery-aware
  + current evidence is a generic synthetic capability fixture and cannot support a real activation trial
  + pure forms can be exhaustively tested without weakening Windows host policy or requiring provider availability

& [Rejected]
  + infer a real activation instance from synthetic SWA-06B1 evidence
  + write a current-SOP registry or activate Pinky boot authority without an exact signed import
  + treat supplied paths snapshots owners or policies as physical observations
  + combine transaction admission with filesystem effects self-review self-signature boot validation or rollback execution
  + reuse the blocked SWA-05 physical fixture grant or infer its candidate selection

& [ExpectedProductEffect]
  + a later minimal writer receives one complete candidate current-state atomicity durability supersession and rollback contract
  + stale source registry or recovery substitutions can be refused before physical contact
  + the product advances from signed-review mechanics to an activation-ready transaction protocol without false completion
